(The map twin of test 812: a map passed as two parameters is one map.)
To 'merge' of a map called first and a map called second.
    For each number from 1 to 20, Set first's "{number}" to number.
    Print "second sees: {second's length}".
    Set second's "via second" to 99.
    Print "first sees: {first's length}".

a map called stock is {"pears": 1}.
'merge' of stock and stock.
Print "stock length: {stock's length}".
a number called last is stock's "via second".
Print "via second: {last}".
